From: Harvey Newstrom <hnewstrom@hnewstrom.ess.harris.com>
Subject: TWINS:  Comparing life-extender and non-extender

Here is a follow-up on comparing my twin brother and I.  Remember that we 
are identical twins, confirmed by genetic testing.  I have been on a 
nutrient life-extension program for over 10 years, eaten a vegetarian diet 
for 8 years, and have always had dynamic optimism.  My brother has not 
become interested in nutrition, eats TV-dinners and meat, and has dynamic 
pessimism.

Someone asked if my brother looked older than I.  (Great question!)  I 
responded that I generally look healthier and sexier, and quoted some 
comments from other people to support this.  I was not sure if I look 
younger or not, because I am not a good judge of age.  I also noted that 
many people could not tell my brother and I apart 10 years ago, but now now 
one confuses us.  We have obviously grown to look different, but still 
obviously twins.

I have a family photograph here, which I am carefully studying to note 
differences between my twin and I...

I have come up with an interesting observation, and I now believe that I do 
look younger than my twin!  We have one other brother who is four years 
older than us.  He looks very similar to us, only older.  After carefully 
examining a family picture to determine how my twin and I differ, I noticed 
that my twin looks like a cross between my older brother and I.  When 
comparing my older brother with us twins, it seems obvious that my twin 
looks more like my older brother than I do.  He still looks closer to me 
than to my older brother, but it may be that the differences that have 
appeared are due to aging.

My brothers have wrinkles around their face from smiling, mine are 
difficult to detect even though I seem to be grinning even wider.  My 
brothers seem to have thinner hair which is a darker color.  My hair seems 
thicker and lighter in color.  (I avoid sunlight, so it is not bleached.  
My older brother works outside in the sun all day.)  My two brothers have 
slight skin tone variations on their faces and neck.  My skin seems more 
uniform in color.  Both my brothers have a wrinkle on either side of the 
nose, under the cheek bones.  I cannot detect this wrinkle on me.  Both my 
brothers have a slight wrinkle on their ear lobes, while I do not seem to 
have this.  The whites of my eyes seem to be brighter, and the pupils seem 
more distinct.  The outline of the pupils seems more clearly defined in my 
eyes.  I also think I can detect slight sags in the neck under the chin on 
my two brothers which I do not have, but these could be shadows.  My 
eyebrows seem to be fuller than my two brothers.  My posture seems to be 
better, but I don't believe I generally have good posture.  My brothers 
both have bags and shadows under their eyes, I cannot detect any puffiness 
or darkness under my eyes.

My older brother and I drink, and my twin does not.  I get carded to prove 
my age all the time.  My brother who is 4 years older never gets carded.  
My twin does not drink, and therefore does not know.

(P.S. Now I'm really in a good mood!  This group is great for my dynamic 
optimism!)
