Subject: What is a Singularity? (was: Technology/Politics)

I define the 'Singularity' as the unique time in history of most
rapid technological change.  If progress continues ad infinitum, then
it would be the asymptote of the hyperbola.  If progress slows
down (as I expect) by approaching fundamental physical limits
(speed of light, planck's constant), then it is the time when the
slope of progress is highest.

