Subject: Intermittent supplement use?

I couldn't take pills for many years due to gagging on them.  I
wanted to take supplements, however, and I learned to do it by
starting with Vitamin E capsules (200IU small spheres) mixed
in with food I was eating (I just had to learn not to chew
between adding the capsule to the food already in my mouth
and swallowing).  I gradually worked down what I added to the
pills until I could swallow a pill with just some water, then
worked up to bigger pills (like the big horse multivitamin
pills I swallow now)  Along the way, I learned how to maneuver
the pill to the back of my toungue, add water, tilt head back,
and swallow.  If you do it right, you wash the pill down with
the swallow of water, so it feels like you are just swallowing
some water.

The whole learning process has taken me 5 years to get to where
I can take big pills in the morning without hardly thinking
about it (I'm on autopilot in the morning)

