I have considered it obvious for some years now that we will soon
be able to enhance our pets with at least one AI application which
will change the way we think of them:

speech synthesizers etc.

When your pet can speak to you in plain English (or whatever),
you will finally be sure of things like "I want to go out NOW!"
which are already usually but not always obvious.  I suspect
it will be longer (perhaps much longer) before more than simple
statements regarding state or desire for state change are
translatable.  Eventually, however, a pet with a combined
voice recognition / natural language understanding / translation /
speech synthesis / common-sense (general world knowledge) system /
etc. may be able to converse with us.  This will further confuse
the issue of personhood.  It will mean that formerly silent
witnesses to a wide variety of acts will be able to speak up.
Who knows what else...

Can you imagine a conversation between a dog and a cat?
In some ways, I bet the gap between them is wider than
that between either of them and humans.

I don't consider any entity to be my equal unless and until
it re-creates itself to a significant extent as an act of
conscious will.  That will apply to artificially evolved pets
in the future just as it does to naturally evolved humans now.
